<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 06:38:45 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>France and Spain battle vast wildfires as fresh heatwave approaches</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260727-france-and-spain-battle-vast-wildfires-as-fresh-heatwave-approaches</link><description>
Firefighters are continuing to battle huge forest fires across France and Spain on Monday, as authorities warned that another heatwave could bring temperatures of up to 40C to the already scorched wine-growing region around Bordeaux.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b3a2b2-8983-11f1-8ce6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3987H6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b3a2b2-8983-11f1-8ce6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3987H6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08ea9bda-8983-11f1-b9cc-e5a49bdb74b3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 06:36:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b3a2b2-8983-11f1-8ce6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3987H6.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Threatened by fire, Bordeaux is 'ready for anything': mayor</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260727-threatened-by-fire-bordeaux-is-ready-for-anything-mayor</link><description>
The mayor of Bordeaux in southwest France said on Sunday authorities had no current plans to evacuate the UNESCO-listed city due to raging forest fires but were "ready for anything." 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5643fa6c-8838-11f1-887c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-25T141114Z-776257927-RC2XKMARM7UI-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-EVACUATION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5643fa6c-8838-11f1-887c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-25T141114Z-776257927-RC2XKMARM7UI-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-EVACUATION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82fc7b50-88fc-11f1-8151-73a8bbe5631a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 06:37:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5643fa6c-8838-11f1-887c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-25T141114Z-776257927-RC2XKMARM7UI-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-EVACUATION.jpg">REUTERS - Manon Cruz</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Main suspect in Berlin Pride attack shot dead by German police forces</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-several-people-are-injured-at-berlin-s-lgbtq-march-after-a-car-drives-into-the-crowd</link><description>
The suspect in the deadly Berlin Pride attack that left one person dead and 29 injured was shot and killed by police during a confrontation on Sunday in a suburb of the city, authorities said. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/466cc732-8918-11f1-b6e7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ALLEMAGNE-POLICE-BERLIN-OPERATION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/466cc732-8918-11f1-b6e7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ALLEMAGNE-POLICE-BERLIN-OPERATION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24d70508-8871-11f1-b3a1-f192ae8cdfbf</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 21:42:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/466cc732-8918-11f1-b6e7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ALLEMAGNE-POLICE-BERLIN-OPERATION.jpg">REUTERS - Christian Mang</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Tadej Pogacar wins a record-equaling fifth Tour de France title</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260726-pogacar-wins-record-equalling-fifth-tour-de-france-2</link><description>
Tadej Pogacar claimed his record-equalling fifth Tour de France title as Mathieu van der Poel won a sensational 21st and final stage around Paris on Sunday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbfc5b4-8922-11f1-926e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-26T180350Z-1735657331-UP1EM7Q1DVENF-RTRMADP-3-CYCLING-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbfc5b4-8922-11f1-926e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-26T180350Z-1735657331-UP1EM7Q1DVENF-RTRMADP-3-CYCLING-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">18b2eb86-8914-11f1-92d7-816556919eec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 19:06:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbfc5b4-8922-11f1-926e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-26T180350Z-1735657331-UP1EM7Q1DVENF-RTRMADP-3-CYCLING-FRANCE.jpg">© Stephanie Lecocq / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>How slavery money built the Élysée, France’s presidential residence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260726-how-slavery-money-built-the-%C3%A9lys%C3%A9e-france-s-presidential-residence</link><description>
What would become the Élysée Palace, the official residence of the French president, was built three centuries ago with a fortune amassed in the slave trade. As France grapples with its legacy of slavery, calls are mounting for the country to acknowledge this and other traces of the past.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/008a592a-10cd-11ea-9d6c-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-07t140652z_290399344_rc11562d3900_rtrmadp_3_france-business.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/008a592a-10cd-11ea-9d6c-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-07t140652z_290399344_rc11562d3900_rtrmadp_3_france-business.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b9f2020-85e6-11f1-a515-b57224aab095</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 16:50:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/008a592a-10cd-11ea-9d6c-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2019-07-07t140652z_290399344_rc11562d3900_rtrmadp_3_france-business.jpg">© REUTERS/Regis Duvignau </source><dc:creator>Jessica Phelan</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfire situation in France ‘remains very unfavourable’, interior minister says</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260725-french-pm-orders-deployment-of-a400m-military-transport-plane-to-help-battle-fires</link><description>
French Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez said on Sunday the wildfire situation in southwestern France was still "very unfavourable”. More than 300,000 people fled wildfires raging across France and Spain on Saturday as worsening conditions forced fresh evacuations. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2e5298d2-88de-11f1-9192-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3894LL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2e5298d2-88de-11f1-9192-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3894LL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b8f5b28-8803-11f1-b97f-915c535ddd7f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:54:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2e5298d2-88de-11f1-9192-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3894LL.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>UNESCO adds France's D-Day landing beaches, Greece's Mount Olympus to World Heritage List</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260726-unesco-adds-france-s-d-day-landing-beaches-greece-s-mount-olympus-to-world-heritage-list</link><description>
UNESCO has added France’s D-Day landing beaches and Greece’s Mount Olympus to its World Heritage List, during a UN committee meeting in South Korea reviewing dozens of nominations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9db453f8-2401-11ef-8787-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U88K6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9db453f8-2401-11ef-8787-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U88K6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4dd50868-88d2-11f1-a139-576c178f8b76</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 10:30:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9db453f8-2401-11ef-8787-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U88K6.jpg">© AFP - -Imperial War Museum</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ecowas greenlights $25bn Nigeria-Morocco mega gas pipeline</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260726-ecowas-greenlights-25bn-mega-gas-pipeline-nigeria-morocco</link><description>
West African leaders have approved plans for a gas pipeline linking Nigeria to Morocco, marking a major political milestone for one of Africa's most ambitious infrastructure projects.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">596d58c6-851f-11f1-8b17-3366361549e6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 08:54:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg">AFP - FLORIAN PLAUCHEUR</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>No snakes in church and don't eat the frogs: the weird world of US animal laws</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260726-no-snakes-in-church-and-don-t-eat-the-frogs-the-weird-world-of-us-animal-laws</link><description>
A few keywords in a search engine will bring up any number of strange laws involving animals in the United States. Many are urban myths: there is no law specifically prohibiting driving a car in Massachusetts with a gorilla in the back seat, although no one would dispute that would be a questionable idea. Others, however, are very real. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e73070-74dc-11f1-a795-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Handling-serpents-at-the-Pentecostal-Church-of-God-Kentucky-by-Russell-Lee-NARA-541335.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e73070-74dc-11f1-a795-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Handling-serpents-at-the-Pentecostal-Church-of-God-Kentucky-by-Russell-Lee-NARA-541335.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e4e53e2-850a-11f1-84e4-4db1a4532f94</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 19:21:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/74e73070-74dc-11f1-a795-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Handling-serpents-at-the-Pentecostal-Church-of-God-Kentucky-by-Russell-Lee-NARA-541335.jpg">© Russell Lee, National Archives and Records Administration NAID 541335, via Wikicommons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Trauma and taboos: how Portugal takes care of migrants' mental health</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260726-trauma-and-taboos-how-portugal-takes-care-of-migrants-mental-health</link><description>
Migration is increasingly essential to Portugal's economy, but the mental health of many new arrivals to the country is affected by the trauma of what they have left behind, long and arduous journeys, and the racism that greets them, fuelled by far-right rhetoric. In addition, mental health treatment is often impeded by cultural and linguistic barriers. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ac2a64a-6be8-11f1-bc30-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/What-Health-Portugal-sant%C3%A9-mentale.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ac2a64a-6be8-11f1-bc30-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/What-Health-Portugal-sant%C3%A9-mentale.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a991009e-85c1-11f1-a361-7373ca996252</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:59:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ac2a64a-6be8-11f1-bc30-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/What-Health-Portugal-sant%C3%A9-mentale.jpeg">© Sofia Peyssonneau / Fondação Aga Khan</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal ready to show ‘what it is capable of’ at Dakar 2026 Youth Olympics</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260726-senegal-ready-to-show-what-it-is-capable-of-at-dakar-2026-youth-olympics</link><description>
With venues nearing completion and public enthusiasm growing, Dakar 2026 chief organiser Ibrahima Wade tells RFI that Senegal is ready to make Olympic history when the Youth Games begin on 31 October.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c11d46d6-866c-11f1-8b0d-07709273a6e7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 05:14:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg">AFP - SEYLLOU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Climate change 'exacerbating' drought across Europe, scientists say</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260725-climate-change-exacerbating-drought-across-europe-scientists-say</link><description>
Climate change is exacerbating drought in Europe as extreme heat evaporates water supplies, scientists said in a study published this week, with low water levels disrupting shipping, farming and industry in countries including Romania and Greece.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33dfd932-8437-11f1-a066-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T071512Z-1618978233-RC28HMARUIOU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-ROMANIA-DROUGHT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33dfd932-8437-11f1-a066-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T071512Z-1618978233-RC28HMARUIOU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-ROMANIA-DROUGHT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b5aee396-8675-11f1-8500-07980066211b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:58:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33dfd932-8437-11f1-a066-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T071512Z-1618978233-RC28HMARUIOU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-ROMANIA-DROUGHT.jpg">© Inquam Photos / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran seeks to 'sow confusion among Gulf states' by targeting Bahrain and Kuwait</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-iran-seeks-to-sow-confusion-among-gulf-states-by-targeting-bahrain-and-kuwait</link><description>
As Iranian drones and missiles target Bahrain and Kuwait, RFI spoke with Mahdi Ghuloom of the Dubai-based ORF Middle East think tank, who believes long-standing tensions, the small size of the two countries and divisions over how the Gulf should respond are playing their part in this development. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0024bd0e-8434-11f1-be61-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2J77CU-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0024bd0e-8434-11f1-be61-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2J77CU-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7dd28f3e-8681-11f1-8344-157a6b6090b8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:22:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0024bd0e-8434-11f1-be61-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2J77CU-1.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>More health workers strike as Ebola cases in Congo near 3,000, including over 1,300 deaths</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260725-more-health-workers-strike-as-ebola-cases-in-congo-near-3-000-including-over-1-300-deaths</link><description>
Health workers at an Ebola treatment center in eastern Congo went on strike Saturday over payment issues, disrupting care for patients in the epicenter of the country’s rapidly growing outbreak.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a0aa694-8833-11f1-a8ad-1172a0685593</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:21:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg">AP Photo/Dirole Lotsima Dieudonn - Dirole Lotsima Dieudonne</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Israel's move to recognise Armenian genocide stalls under regional pressure</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260725-israel-s-move-to-recognise-armenian-genocide-stalls-under-regional-pressure</link><description>
The Israeli parliament's decision to postpone a vote on recognising the Armenian genocide by Ottoman Turkey is being seen as a triumph for regional diplomacy, as Azerbaijan in particular seeks to avert a further escalation in tensions between its close allies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dfc0b862-8756-11f1-8b1e-b11ae43ab3b1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 11:44:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Haitians at home and abroad fear fallout from end of US protection</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-haitians-in-port-au-prince-and-new-york-fear-fallout-from-end-of-us-protectionn</link><description>
Concern is mounting in Haiti and in the United States ahead of the planned end of Temporary Protected Status for Haitians on 27 July, which could leave nearly 350,000 people at risk of deportation from the US.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/263c440c-871e-11f1-bf13-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26190726418960.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/263c440c-871e-11f1-bf13-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26190726418960.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e873a4d2-8748-11f1-89df-852f3d9356bc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:18:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/263c440c-871e-11f1-bf13-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26190726418960.jpg">© Gregory Bull / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>NGOs take France to court over companies’ links to Israeli settlements</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260725-ngos-take-france-to-court-over-companies-links-to-israeli-settlements</link><description>
Five NGOs on Wednesday filed a case before France’s highest administrative court, seeking a ruling that would oblige the French government to take measures preventing French companies and economic institutions from conducting commercial activities in Israeli settlements.
